From: OCCTSwift ecosystem <noreply@secondmouse.au>
Subject: [PATCH] Modeling Algorithms - IntTools_FaceFace::Perform refuses a face without a
 surface

IntTools_FaceFace::Perform reads the surface of each face and goes on to use it.
CorrectSurfaceBoundaries calls Bounds on `BRep_Tool::Surface(theFace)`, which is a null handle for
a face without a surface. Such a face is legal (BRepCheck_Face reports BRepCheck_NoSurface for it),
and BOPAlgo_CheckerSI runs this class against every face that is not one of the four types it skips
(plane, cylinder, cone, sphere), a face without a surface included. BRepAlgoAPI_Check, and so
BOPAlgo_CheckerSI at the self-interference level, die on such a face when it carries a wire, in
CorrectSurfaceBoundaries.

Perform now returns with IsDone false for a face without a surface, which is what every other
reason for not finishing already does and what the callers test. The checker then reports no
self-interference for it, and the shape, invalid on other grounds, answers false.

Measured on a face with no surface and a wire, each entry point in its own process: BRepAlgoAPI_Check
of the shape, BRepAlgoAPI_Check of a box and the shape, and BOPAlgo_CheckerSI at level 5 died with
SIGSEGV before and answer after (false, false, no errors). Fuse, Common, Cut and Section of a box
and the shape do not reach this class, since they reject the argument first, and are unchanged.

Upstream IR rewrote the class this route goes through (BOPAlgo_FaceSelfIntersect, #1640) with an
explicit null test of the surface, so the route is closed there, but CorrectSurfaceBoundaries
itself still dereferences the handle.

Tracked as SecondMouseAU/OCCTSwift#3509.

---
diff --git a/src/ModelingAlgorithms/TKBO/IntTools/IntTools_FaceFace.cxx b/src/ModelingAlgorithms/TKBO/IntTools/IntTools_FaceFace.cxx
--- a/src/ModelingAlgorithms/TKBO/IntTools/IntTools_FaceFace.cxx
+++ b/src/ModelingAlgorithms/TKBO/IntTools/IntTools_FaceFace.cxx
@@ -343,6 +343,12 @@ void IntTools_FaceFace::Perform(const TopoDS_Face& aF1,
   myFace1 = aF1;
   myFace2 = aF2;
 
+  // a face without a surface has nothing to intersect
+  if (BRep_Tool::Surface(myFace1).IsNull() || BRep_Tool::Surface(myFace2).IsNull())
+  {
+    return;
+  }
+
   const BRepAdaptor_Surface& aBAS1  = myContext->SurfaceAdaptor(myFace1);
   const BRepAdaptor_Surface& aBAS2  = myContext->SurfaceAdaptor(myFace2);
   GeomAbs_SurfaceType        aType1 = aBAS1.GetType();
